  "rule": "the interval a prediction states is the prediction times two multiples, taken from the ratios of hidden over predicted on the training looks, every look with a positive prediction counted and a look that flagged nothing counted with a ratio of zero. Two-sided, the multiples are the 5th and the 95th percentile and hold 90 percent between them. When the 5th percentile is zero, which happens as soon as more than one training look in twenty flagged nothing, nothing is cut off below, and the 95th percentile would hold 95 percent: the interval is then one-sided, from zero to the 90th percentile. It starts at zero because cloud is not known, and an interval that could not hold an empty pass would claim more than the record supports.",
